{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "03YZ", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-examples-sheaves}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a3a6b314aff006a762f72c4a683545640eebcb0b0565d0b85e9b13d12f05cf09", "source_text": "Examples of sheaves", "source_text_hash": "sha256:13e787a1397fbd028cada097c127057ea98460fa940db7ff7ef4b625cde9000a", "unit_id": "tag:03YZ:title"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03YZ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\tau$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0004": "$S_\\tau$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-big-small}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-representable-sheaf-fpqc}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{remark-fpqc-finest}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0318854576aec28b279e2c05f073c74f89882471f055848c5dd957c1fae9f965", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fa269f7cade692371efeffb8da714c6b5c4a9477e1a0b229227e010c66b5b105", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be as in Section <REF_0001>.\nWe have already seen that any representable presheaf is a sheaf on\n<MATH_0003> or <MATH_0004>, see\nLemma <REF_0002>\nand\nRemark <REF_0003>.\nHere are some special cases.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5787191129a95d74fc44ca37faea4cbc7e56b76ba0be0111aafbd4213eeb5bb2", "unit_id": "tag:03YZ:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03YZ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0002": "$S_\\tau$", "MATH_0003": "$T \\mapsto \\Gamma(T, \\mathcal{O}_T)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathbf{G}_a$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathbf{G}_{a, S}$", "MATH_0007": "$T \\mapsto \\Gamma(T, \\mathcal{O}^*_T)$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_S^*$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathbf{G}_m$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathbf{G}_{m, S}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}/n\\mathbf{Z}}$", "MATH_0012": "$U \\mapsto \\mathbf{Z}/n\\mathbf{Z}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-big-small}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-additive-sheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e50605461b63ef845528f0c9b53f34dbcdf1b741f33c4d20915bda193b494c75", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5bcc1a7d2913e4969a4b0636e2801b6cee58f6aeae069e49d6eab5453d07edb4", "source_text": "On any of the sites <MATH_0001> or <MATH_0002> of\nSection <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The sheaf <MATH_0003> is denoted\n<MATH_0004>, or <MATH_0005>, or <MATH_0006> if we\nwant to indicate the base scheme.\n<STRUCT_0003> Similarly, the sheaf\n<MATH_0007> is denoted <MATH_0008>, or\n<MATH_0009>, or <MATH_0010> if we want\nto indicate the base scheme.\n<STRUCT_0004> The <TEXTITOPEN_0001>constant sheaf<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> <MATH_0011> on any\nsite is the sheafification of the constant presheaf\n<MATH_0012>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:08f2c93eb98dfceafdc76f46ea830589c380d195be27799ed9b7555929a96a73", "unit_id": "tag:03P4:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03YZ", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathbf{G}_{a, S}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathbf{G}_{m, S}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathbf{Z}/n\\mathbf{Z}_S$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\mathbf{Z}/n\\mathbf{Z})_S$", "MATH_0005": "$n$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-quasi-coherent}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{groupoids-section-group-schemes}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{groupoids-example-constant-group}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d6644d6ce5a64a2f2dd4a7172a9c4ff3f695a190d525a60ed14a451524006ad8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d84769db42bbdf4dfc579179a38950c52d447a8489cd07ccb8827f5ba8539d2d", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe first is a sheaf by\nTheorem <REF_0001>\nfor example. The second is a sub presheaf of the first, which is easily seen\nto be a sheaf itself. The third is a sheaf by definition.\nNote that each of these sheaves is representable.\nThe first and second by the schemes <MATH_0001> and\n<MATH_0002>, see\nGroupoids, Section <REF_0002>.\nThe third by the finite <ACCENT_0001>tale group scheme <MATH_0003>\nsometimes denoted <MATH_0004>\nwhich is just <MATH_0005> copies of <MATH_0006> endowed\nwith the obvious group scheme structure over <MATH_0007>, see\nGroupoids, Example <REF_0003>\nand the following remark.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a8fb68ff25d606bab5f8bd190101b865c0b05599227418c14d4c08c6e8204ebf", "unit_id": "tag:03YZ:prose-0002"}
